Śatrughna marches alone and reaches Vālmīki āśrama after two nights --- Vālmīki welcomes Śatrughna with seat water food --- Śatrughna asks whose ancient sacrifice ground lies nearby --- Vālmīki names ancestor king Sudāsa son Mitrasaha Saudāsa --- Saudāsa kills one tiger-formed man-eating rākṣasa while hunting --- Surviving rākṣasa vows revenge and vanishes --- Rākṣasa disguised as Vasiṣṭha then cook serves human flesh --- Vasiṣṭha curses Saudāsa then limits curse to twelve years --- Saudāsa endures curse regains kingdom and protects subjects --- Śatrughna hears tale and enters leaf hut